# Shared contact pool (Apollo credit saver)

A shared Google Sheet caches enriched contacts across everyone using this
system. Before spending Apollo credits on a company, check the pool; after
enriching, push new contacts back so the next person skips Apollo.

**If the pool is not configured** (`google.shared_pool_spreadsheet_id` unset
and no `OUTREACH_SHARED_POOL_SPREADSHEET_ID` env), the commands print a skip
message and exit — do nothing special, just proceed with normal Apollo. Do NOT
treat that as an error.

## In every campaign

1. **Before Apollo discovery/enrich**, look up the company:

```bash
node scripts/pool-lookup.mjs --domain company.com --company "Company" --slug <slug>
```

   - Exit 0 = HIT: it wrote `output/enrich/<slug>.json` in the normal enrich
     shape. Reuse those contacts and SKIP Apollo search + enrich. Policy is
     SUPPLEMENT: if the pooled contacts don't cover the team the JD needs, run
     the normal Apollo buckets only for the gap, then push (step 2).
   - Exit 3 = MISS: run the normal Apollo discovery + enrich as usual.
   - Exit 2 = pool not configured: proceed normally, no pool.

2. **After a fresh Apollo enrich** (i.e. any time you spent credits), push the
   results so others benefit:

```bash
node scripts/pool-push.mjs --enrich output/enrich/<slug>.json --domain company.com --company "Company"
```

   Skip this when the enrich file came from the pool (it self-detects
   `source=shared_pool` and no-ops).

3. **After replies get classified / after shipping** (any time outcomes change),
   contribute reply + bounce + send signals so everyone benefits:

```bash
node scripts/pool-sync-outcomes.mjs
```

   This reads YOUR sheet (Queue/Archive/Blacklist/Replies) and writes back only
   anonymous signals: a reply category (positive/referral/negative/auto_reply/
   unclear), a `do_not_send` flag for bounced/opted-out emails, and the WEEK
   each contact was emailed (for collision avoidance). Reply text is never
   shared. A good habit: run it right after `classify-replies.mjs`.

4. **After writing new contact briefs**, share the research:

```bash
node scripts/pool-push-briefs.mjs --slug $SLUG
```

   Only contact research is shared — sections about proof selection / draft
   guidance and any line naming you are stripped automatically. Never hand-edit
   a brief into the pool to add pitch advice.

## Automatic behaviors (don't fight these)

- **Do-not-send suppression:** `pool-lookup` drops any contact another friend
  saw bounce or opt out, so you never draft to a dead address. It reports how
  many it suppressed.
- **Reply gist:** pooled contacts that previously got a reply carry
  `pool_reply_status` in the enrich file (and print `[reply seen: ...]`).
  Prioritize a contact with a `positive` gist when selecting/drafting.
- **Collision avoidance (IMPORTANT):** contacts emailed by anyone in the pool
  within 14 days print `[RECENT OUTREACH: ~Nd ago]` and a COLLISION WARNING.
  Two people hitting the same recruiter in the same fortnight reads as a spam
  wave and costs the whole group its reply rate — pick a different contact at
  that company, or use `--exclude-recent` to drop them. Only override when the
  user explicitly wants that contact.
- **Shared briefs:** on a hit, `pool-lookup` writes any pooled briefs into
  `output/contact-briefs/<slug>/`. If a brief file already exists for a contact,
  do NOT launch a brief subagent for them — read the file instead. Shared briefs
  contain contact research only, so you still choose the proof and CTA yourself.
- **Backfill on setup:** `setup-shared-pool.mjs` auto-runs `pool-backfill.mjs`
  (all past `output/enrich/*.json`), `pool-sync-outcomes.mjs`, and
  `pool-push-briefs.mjs`, so joining the pool seeds a person's entire history.
  Re-runnable; pass `--no-backfill` to skip.

## Rules

- The pool is ANONYMOUS: never add, store, or display any field identifying who
  contributed a contact OR who observed an outcome. The scripts already omit
  this — don't add it. The shared reply signal is a category only, never text.
- Cached emails can be stale; that's fine — the exporter re-verifies and drops
  bad addresses at export time. Use `--max-age-days N` on lookup to ignore very
  old rows if desired.
- One-time setup per person: `node scripts/setup-shared-pool.mjs --id <SHEET_ID>`
  (see `SETUP_SHARED_POOL.md`).
